            "sectionHeading": "Inheritance Tax Summary",
            "quote": "Currently, your assets are below your allowance of \u00A3500,000 meaning you have no Inheritance Tax liability. However, on receipt of the inheritance this will take you over the limit."
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "There are several strategies to help reduce your IHT liability, including: Trusts - Placing assets in trust to remove them from your taxable estate. Gifts \u0026 Lifetime Transfers - Making tax-efficient gifts to reduce the value of your estate. Whole of Life Plans - Using life insurance to cover any expected IHT bill.",
          "topic": "IHTMitigationStrategies",
          "isClientSpecific": true,
          "linkedObjectiveIds": [
            "OBJ6"
          ],
          "provenance": {
            "assertionStatus": "Stated",
            "modality": "Intended",
            "documentId": "Suitability report 2026.md",
            "documentCategory": "I_RecommendationsAndAdvice",
            "pageNumbers": [
              4
            ],
            "sectionHeading": "Inheritance Tax Summary"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Historically, pensions have not formed part of your estate for IHT purposes, making them a valuable estate planning tool. However, legislation has now been passed to change this. From 6 April 2027, most unused defined contribution pensions and death benefits (such as drawdown funds and uncrystallised pots) will be included in your taxable estate for IHT. Exceptions include pensions paid to a surviving spouse or civil partner, dependents\u0027 scheme pensions, and death-in-service benefits.",
          "topic": "PensionIHTChange",
          "isClientSpecific": false,
          "linkedObjectiveIds": [
            "OBJ6"
          ],
          "provenance": {
            "assertionStatus": "Stated",
            "modality": "Actual",
            "documentId": "Suitability report 2026.md",
            "documentCategory": "I_RecommendationsAndAdvice",
            "pageNumbers": [
              4
            ],
            "sectionHeading": "Inheritance Tax Summary",
            "quote": "From 6 April 2027, most unused defined contribution pensions and death benefits (such as drawdown funds and uncrystallised pots) will be included in your taxable estate for IHT."
          }
        }
      ],
