          "text": "Death benefits paid tax-free if you die before age 75; subject to beneficiary marginal tax rate if you die on or after age 75",
          "topic": "DeathBenefitsTax",
          "isClientSpecific": true,
          "linkedObjectiveIds": [
            "OBJ6"
          ],
          "provenance": {
            "assertionStatus": "Stated",
            "modality": "Actual",
            "documentId": "Suitability report 2026.md",
            "documentCategory": "I_RecommendationsAndAdvice",
            "pageNumbers": [
              20
            ],
            "quote": "Where your nominees withdraw from the proceeds it will be tax free should you die before age 75. Where your death occurs on or after age 75 those payments will be subject to the nominee\u0027s marginal rate of tax."
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "From 6 April 2027, IHT treatment of pensions changes with most unused defined contribution pensions and death benefits included in taxable estate except where paid to spouse/civil partner, dependents\u0027 scheme pensions, or death-in-service benefits",
          "topic": "IHTTreatmentChange",
          "isClientSpecific": true,
          "linkedObjectiveIds": [
            "OBJ6"
          ],
          "provenance": {
            "assertionStatus": "Stated",
            "modality": "Actual",
            "documentId": "Suitability report 2026.md",
            "documentCategory": "I_RecommendationsAndAdvice",
            "pageNumbers": [
              4,
              12
            ],
            "quote": "From 6 April 2027, most unused defined contribution pensions and death benefits (such as drawdown funds and uncrystallised pots) will be included in your taxable estate for IHT. Exceptions include pensions paid to a surviving spouse or civil partner, dependents\u0027 scheme pensions, and death-in-service benefits."
          }
        }
      ],
      "provenance": {
        "assertionStatus": "Stated",
